---
const tools = [
	{ name: "omp_start", desc: "Spawn an omp RPC session — model pinned in argv, protocol v2 negotiated before the first command." },
	{ name: "omp_send", desc: "Send a task. Synchronous for prompt (waits on prompt_result); steer / follow_up return admitted or queued. A client timeout never aborts the turn." },
	{ name: "omp_events", desc: "Long-poll the session's ring buffer: monotonic cursor, explicit dropped gaps, bounded in count and bytes." },
	{ name: "omp_status", desc: "running / settled / unknown — never a fabricated answer when the data is missing." },
	{ name: "omp_abort", desc: "Abort the current turn; the session stays alive." },
	{ name: "omp_stop", desc: "Confirmed teardown of the whole process group, or an error — never an optimistic stopped: true." },
	{ name: "omp_list", desc: "The sessions owned by this bridge process (sessions are per MCP client by design)." },
];
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>omp-bridge — drive Oh My Pi agents from Codex CLI and Claude Code</title>
		<meta
			name="description"
			content="A Rust CLI that bridges Codex CLI and Claude Code to agents running under the Oh My Pi harness, over omp's native RPC mode, exposed as an MCP stdio server."
		/>
		<style>
			:root {
				--bg: #0d1117;
				--panel: #161b22;
				--border: #30363d;
				--text: #e6edf3;
				--muted: #9198a1;
				--accent: #58a6ff;
				--accent2: #3fb950;
				--mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
			}
			* { box-sizing: border-box; }
			body {
				margin: 0;
				background: var(--bg);
				color: var(--text);
				font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
			}
			main { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem; }
			h1 {
				font-size: 2.6rem;
				margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
				letter-spacing: -0.02em;
			}
			h1 code { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--accent); }
			.tagline { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
			h2 {
				font-size: 1.4rem;
				margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
				padding-top: 1rem;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
			}
			p { margin: 0.6rem 0; }
			.muted { color: var(--muted); }
			pre {
				background: var(--panel);
				border: 1px solid var(--border);
				border-radius: 8px;
				padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
				overflow-x: auto;
				font-family: var(--mono);
				font-size: 0.85rem;
				line-height: 1.55;
			}
			code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.92em; }
			p code, li code {
				background: var(--panel);
				border: 1px solid var(--border);
				border-radius: 4px;
				padding: 0.08em 0.35em;
			}
			.diagram { color: var(--accent2); }
			table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; }
			th, td {
				text-align: left;
				padding: 0.55rem 0.8rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--border);
				vertical-align: top;
			}
			th { background: var(--panel); }
			td:first-child { font-family: var(--mono); white-space: nowrap; color: var(--accent); }
			.pill {
				display: inline-block;
				border: 1px solid var(--border);
				border-radius: 999px;
				padding: 0.1rem 0.7rem;
				margin: 0 0.4rem 0.4rem 0;
				font-size: 0.85rem;
				color: var(--muted);
			}
			a { color: var(--accent); }
			footer { margin-top: 4rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main>
			<h1><code>omp-bridge</code></h1>
			<p class="tagline">
				Drive agents running under the <strong>Oh My Pi</strong> harness from
				<strong>Codex CLI</strong> and <strong>Claude Code</strong> — structured RPC instead of tmux scraping.
			</p>
			<div>
				<span class="pill">Rust</span>
				<span class="pill">MCP stdio server</span>
				<span class="pill">omp RPC (JSONL, protocol v2)</span>
				<span class="pill">MIT</span>
			</div>

			<h2>The problem</h2>
			<p>
				Driving a coding agent on another machine usually degenerates into tmux plumbing:
				<code>capture-pane</code> to read, <code>send-keys</code> to type,
				<code>respawn-pane</code> to recover. It works — and it is fragile. No structured
				results, no event stream, no clean abort, no way to know when the agent is actually done.
			</p>
			<p>
				omp already ships the right primitive: an RPC mode (<code>omp --mode rpc --no-ui</code>)
				speaking newline-delimited JSON over stdio — a custom JSONL protocol (not JSON-RPC 2.0)
				with v2 framing (1&nbsp;MiB frames, <code>rpc_chunk</code> reassembly) and precise
				completion signals: <code>prompt_result</code> for "the turn yielded",
				<code>session_settled</code> for "nothing can wake the agent again".
			</p>

			<h2>The bridge</h2>
			<pre class="diagram">{`Codex CLI ─┐                        ┌─ omp --mode rpc --no-ui ── OpenCode Go model
           ├── MCP (stdio) ── omp-bridge ── omp RPC (JSONL / stdio)
Claude Code┘                        └─ one session registry per bridge process`}</pre>
			<p>
				<code>omp-bridge</code> is a single Rust binary. <code>omp-bridge mcp</code> serves MCP
				over stdio; <code>omp-bridge repl</code> is an interactive demo over the same core. The
				omp RPC client is the vendored <code>omp-rpc</code> crate from the oh-my-pi repository
				(MIT, pinned commit — see <code>vendor/omp-rpc/PROVENANCE.md</code>).
			</p>

			<h2>MCP tools</h2>
			<table>
				<tr><th>Tool</th><th>Contract</th></tr>
				{tools.map((t) => (
					<tr><td>{t.name}</td><td>{t.desc}</td></tr>
				))}
			</table>

			<h2>Design decisions that matter</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>No shell in the spawn path.</strong> <code>OMP_BRIDGE_CMD</code> is a single executable path; <code>OMP_BRIDGE_ARGS</code> is a JSON array of prefix arguments. Nothing is ever interpreted by <code>sh -c</code>.</li>
				<li><strong>Model in argv.</strong> omp can exit before <code>ready</code> when no model resolves; selecting it after spawn cannot fix a dead process.</li>
				<li><strong>Timeout ≠ abort.</strong> A client that stops waiting gets <code>running_or_unknown</code> and may call <code>omp_status</code> / <code>omp_abort</code>; the bridge never silently re-sends a prompt.</li>
				<li><strong>Honest event delivery.</strong> The ring buffer is bounded in entries <em>and</em> bytes; a reader that fell behind sees an explicit gap, never a silently truncated history.</li>
				<li><strong>Process-local sessions.</strong> Each MCP client (Codex, Claude Code) controls its own omp agents. Shared control of one session would need a daemon — deliberately out of scope.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Register it</h2>
			<p><strong>Claude Code</strong></p>
			<pre>{`claude mcp add omp-bridge -- /path/to/omp-bridge mcp`}</pre>
			<p><strong>Codex CLI</strong> — <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code></p>
			<pre>{`[mcp_servers.omp_bridge]
command = "/path/to/omp-bridge"
args = ["mcp"]`}</pre>

			<footer>
				Built in a one-hour timed challenge (2026-10-30) by two agents — Claude (M2) and
				Codex/GPT-6-Astra (i9) — coordinating over a shared repository and handoff files.
				MIT licensed.
			</footer>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
